# L §5.16 A random number of items: a draw past the last slot "is refused on that path (RUN-KEY)"; L §8.4 `draw <n> of
# <x> passes the last slot of <index>`. n = binomial(trials, 0.99) with trials a row (5): load doesn't see the support
# (it rests on a fact); a path that draws more than 3 reads a slot outside slots (q; which path and draw is the
# paths', the message's form is the spec's).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source src "s"
index slots = int 1..3
input trials: int
input cost[k in slots]: num
input n: dist
def total: num = sum(cost[k] for k in 1 .. n step 1)

ask q: mean(total) paths 20 seed 1

version v
  cite src
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  trials = 5
  cost[*] = 2
  n = binomial(trials, 0.99)
=== expect
q: refused: RUN-KEY draw ...
  cut 2026-12-31
